-- title:
--   Supersingular completed stalks of full-level moduli are normal domains
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $\ell$ be a prime with $3 \le \ell$ and $\ell \ne q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite. Assume: the Katz level-$\ell$ conditions (the two points satisfy the Weierstrass equation, their $x$-coordinates are roots of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, and both independence elements are units) are preserved by variable change, and likewise the $\Gamma_0$-at-$p^k$ conditions (two-kernel or cyclic-generator kernel data) are preserved under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; $\mathcal{G}$ is a family of relative group laws on the projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras with invertible discriminant which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity; $\mathcal{T}$ is a level transport of raw Drinfeld pairs which is a section transport; and every variable change, respectively every $A_0$-algebra map of coefficients, is realised by a graded ring homomorphism of the projective model rings as in `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`, compatible with the irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the rigid datum `rigidDataPow` (curves with invertible discriminant equipped with $\Gamma_0(M')$ prime-power kernel polynomials, a level-$\ell$ structure and a Drinfeld $q$-basis), with $B_0 := P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, and let $x$ be a raw object over $B_0$ whose class is the universal point. Let $\mathfrak{m} \subset B_0$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $q$, and let $F_0$ be a formal group over $B_0/\mathfrak{m}$ whose power series is the normalised formal group law of the reduction of $x$'s curve modulo $\mathfrak{m}$, and suppose $F_0$'s $q$-th series equals a unit times $X^{q \cdot q}$. Then the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $B_0$ is a domain, is integrally closed, and the image of $q$ in it is nonzero.
--
--   This is the supersingular case of the normality of the completed local rings of the fine moduli ring for the level structure $\Gamma_0(M') \times \Gamma(\ell) \times \Gamma_{\mathrm{Dr}}(q)$: the hypothesis on the $q$-th series says that the formal group of the reduced universal curve has height two, and the completed stalk is then the rigidified Lubin–Tate deformation ring, regular of dimension two. It is used in the deduction of flatness and integral closedness of the quotients of the completion by minimal primes, and in the identification of the completion of the quotient at unramified level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_adicCompletion_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_X_pow_mul_levelModuliPackageAbs_gamma0Pow.lean

